Third-party components
----------------------

None. Monitor has no third-party dependency and no CDN.

Vendored from this project's own kits (same licence, same author), copied verbatim on 26/11/2026:

- web-kit 0.1.0 — docs/play/web-kit.js — the offline shell, storage helpers and PWA registration
- export-kit 1.0.0 — docs/play/export-kit.js — Blob download, used for the archive export

Neither kit is modified. Neither makes a network request.

It does not crawl
-----------------

There is no fetch, no crawler and no url queue in this app. A page arrives only because a person
pasted it, and it is stored with the date it was saved. Every rule shows when it was last run, with the
age in words, so a stale table cannot look live.

The selector grammar is deliberately small — tag, .class, tag.class, #id, tag[attr=value] — and it is
validated when a rule is saved, so a scrape is never run against a rule the app did not understand.
